    <title>Is China Misreading the Moment?</title>
    <link href="https://latifkedi.github.io/ahbar/?item=2026-11-18-75-is-china-misreading-the-moment"/>
    <link rel="related" href="https://www.foreignaffairs.com/united-states/china-misreading-moment"/>
    <id>https://latifkedi.github.io/ahbar/item/2026-11-18-75-is-china-misreading-the-moment</id>
    <updated>2026-11-17T09:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;When U.S. President Donald Trump lands in Shenzhen later this week for the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit, he will sit down with Chinese leader Xi Jinping for the fourth time amid an unexpected détente between Washington and Beijing. The trade war of 2025 is in abeyance, the two governments have announced a relationship of “constructive strategic stability,” and, to the alarm of American allies, Trump and Xi are planning to meet with Russian President Vladimir Putin. Beneath the surface, however, the détente is beginning to crack.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foreignaffairs.com/united-states/china-misreading-moment&quot;&gt;Foreign Affairs&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;strong&gt;Tags:&lt;/strong&gt; #geopolitics #defense-strategy&lt;/p&gt;</summary>
